# 🖥️ Terminal 11 Ultimate — Installation Guide

Welcome to **Terminal 11 Ultimate!**

Terminal 11 Ultimate is a Windows 11-inspired desktop application built with Python. It includes a Start Menu, taskbar, File Explorer, built-in terminal, Settings, Notepad, games, and more!

It supports **Windows 10/11** and **Raspberry Pi 4 running Raspberry Pi OS Desktop**.

## 📥 Step 1 — Download Terminal 11 Ultimate

1. Open this GitHub repository.
2. Click the green **Code** button.
3. Select **Download ZIP**.
4. Extract the downloaded ZIP file.
5. Open the extracted project folder.

Alternatively, you can clone the repository using Git:

```bash
git clone https://github.com/YOUR-USERNAME/Terminal11-Ultimate.git
cd Terminal11-Ultimate
```

Replace `YOUR-USERNAME` with the actual GitHub username of the project owner.

---

## 🪟 Installing on Windows 10/11

### Step 1 — Install Python

1. Visit https://www.python.org/downloads/
2. Download Python for Windows.
3. Install Python.
4. Make sure Python is available from Command Prompt.

Check your installation:

```cmd
py --version
```

### Step 2 — Open Terminal 11

Open Command Prompt in the extracted Terminal 11 project folder.

Run:

```cmd
py terminal11.py
```

Terminal 11 Ultimate should launch!

### Step 3 — Enjoy!

Explore the desktop, open the Start Menu, launch applications, and customize your experience.

**Tip:** Press `F11` to toggle fullscreen mode.

