## 🍓 Installing on Raspberry Pi 4

### Requirements

- Raspberry Pi 4
- Raspberry Pi OS Desktop (64-bit recommended)
- MicroSD card (16 GB minimum; 32 GB recommended)
- Keyboard, mouse, and monitor
- Internet connection

### Step 1 — Install Raspberry Pi OS

1. Download Raspberry Pi Imager from https://www.raspberrypi.com/software/
2. Insert your microSD card into your computer.
3. Open Raspberry Pi Imager.
4. Select **Raspberry Pi 4**.
5. Choose **Raspberry Pi OS (64-bit)** with a desktop.
6. Select your microSD card.
7. Write the operating system to the card.
8. Insert the card into your Raspberry Pi and turn it on.

**Warning:** Flashing the SD card erases its existing contents.

### Step 2 — Update Raspberry Pi OS

Open the Raspberry Pi terminal and run:

```bash
sudo apt update
sudo apt upgrade -y
```

### Step 3 — Install Python and Tkinter

```bash
sudo apt install -y python3 python3-tk git
```

### Step 4 — Download Terminal 11

Clone your GitHub repository:

```bash
git clone https://github.com/YOUR-USERNAME/Terminal11-Ultimate.git
cd Terminal11-Ultimate
```

Alternatively, download the ZIP from GitHub and extract it.

### Step 5 — Launch Terminal 11

```bash
python3 terminal11.py
```

Terminal 11 Ultimate should now open on your Raspberry Pi!

