## ⚡ Optional — Start Terminal 11 Automatically

You can configure Terminal 11 to launch when you log in to Raspberry Pi OS.

Create an autostart directory:

```bash
mkdir -p ~/.config/autostart
```

Open a new desktop launcher file:

```bash
nano ~/.config/autostart/terminal11.desktop
```

Paste the following:

```ini
[Desktop Entry]
Type=Application
Name=Terminal 11 Ultimate
Exec=/usr/bin/python3 /home/YOUR-USERNAME/Terminal11-Ultimate/terminal11.py
Path=/home/YOUR-USERNAME/Terminal11-Ultimate
Terminal=false
```

Replace `YOUR-USERNAME` with your Raspberry Pi username and adjust the file path if necessary.

Save using `Ctrl + O`, press Enter, and exit using `Ctrl + X`.

Restart your Raspberry Pi:

```bash
sudo reboot
```

On desktop environments that support this autostart method, Terminal 11 should launch automatically after login.

